  "name": "BIDS Manager",
  "version": "1.5.2",
  "description": "BIDS Manager prepares neuroimaging data in the Brain Imaging Data Structure (BIDS). It reads raw MRI, MR spectroscopy, PET, EEG, MEG, physiological and eye-tracking recordings, proposes a BIDS name for each one, converts them with the established engines, and then helps you complete, curate, inspect and validate the result.\n\nIt is curation software, not only a converter. Every decision is shown and can be changed before anything is written. The metadata a recording cannot carry is asked for by the BIDS schema itself. Every change is recorded, so curation can be resumed weeks later or undone, and the dataset you share is the one you checked. It runs as a desktop application and from the command line.",
